[[17592186059969 :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y,z$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+y+z &=4 \\\\ x+0y+z &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$"] [17592186060201 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the system is already organized so that the variables are in the order $x,y$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient. \n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$"] [17592186241007 :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y &=5 \\\\ -4x+y &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations: \n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$"] [17592186243890 :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y,z$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}9x+3y-z &=16 \\\\ -8x+4y+0z &=-15 \\\\ 20x-y-3z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 20 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 3 & -1 & 16 \\\\ -8 & 4 & 0 & -15 \\\\ 20 & -1 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$"] [17592186262947 :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient: \n\n$$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-y &=4 \\\\ 8x+0y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$"] [17592186262948 :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=5 \\\\ 5x-9y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations: \n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -9 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$"] [17592186338976 :question/worked-solution "First, we or